    <!-- Non-linear rigid-body-spring-network dynamics: tendon tension ->
         actuation TORQUE (not a solved position target) via the tendon-
         routing Jacobian transpose, reacting against each joint's own
         non-linear spring tau_spring=k1*theta+k2*theta^3 and viscous
         damper tau_damp=c_theta*theta_dot - see
         plugins/rbsn_arm_controller's header comment for the exact
         derivation and class docs.

         k1/k2/c_theta (2026-08, live-tuned via the gz bench harness,
         matching the same open-loop target continuum_arm_pcc/
         continuum_arm_cosserat were calibrated against): starting from a
         linearized estimate near the shared K_theta~=1.611 N*m/rad
         baseline (k1=1.6, k2=0) gave only ~44deg at the calibration step
         (max_tension-saturated single-tendon shorten of 0.036m) - live-
         verified too stiff to reach the target range at this arm's actual
         actuation-torque budget, so k1 was walked down (1.6 -> 0.94 ->
         0.82) until the live response matched. k2=0 (pure linear spring
         sufficed to hit the target once k1 was right; left as an SDF-
         exposed, independently tunable knob for anyone wanting to add
         real strain-hardening at large angles). Live-verified (gz bench
         harness, sim-time-based measurement): 71.8deg reached in 2.21s,
         ~0% overshoot - directly comparable to PCC's 73.9deg/1.91s and
         Cosserat's 78.6deg/2.19s. tendon_stiffness/max_tension reuse
         continuum_arm_cosserat's already-validated tendon actuation model
         (same physical tendon assumptions) - see the plugin block below
         for the exact tuned values.

         effort_limit here is a generous safety clamp on the NET per-joint
         torque (actuation - spring - damping), decoupled from the old PD-
         based max_tension*pitch_radius convention since RBSN's torque
         comes from real dynamics, not a position-tracking ceiling.

         command_filter_omega/max_tendon_rate_m_s: identical values to the
         other two models' CommandShaper (plugins/common/CommandShaper.hpp)
         so all three models share one open-loop command-shaping baseline -
         see docs/continuum_arm_three_model_report.md.

         UPDATE 2026-08 (gravity-sag fix): the above k1=0.82/tendon_
         stiffness=3333/max_tension=120/effort_limit=3.0 were calibrated on
         the bare standalone bench only, which structurally cannot exercise
         off-axis gravity (the bench mounts the arm hanging straight down,
         aligned with gravity, so a symmetric neutral pose feels zero
         gravity torque by construction). Live-verified on
         hillstar_continuum_arm_gripper (the actual flying vehicle, arm +
         gripper_3finger payload at the tip) that a 45deg vehicle pitch -
         which this mission profile commands - put the arm ~29deg off-axis
         from gravity, at k1=0.82, and the arm passively sagged to ~29deg
         even with zero bend commanded. Retuned against a rotated-gravity
         bench variant (world <gravity> rotated 45deg, same effect as
         tilting the mount) with continuum_arm_pcc's own 45deg-tilt passive
         droop (9.7deg, its position-PD holds against gravity far more
         rigidly) as the target: k1 1.611->6.2, c_theta scaled to preserve
         the same damping ratio (0.038->0.095, both propto sqrt(k1)) ->
         10.2deg droop on the bare bench, matches PCC closely. That much
         stiffer spring crushed reach (36mm shorten: 62deg -> 14deg), so
         tendon_stiffness/max_tension/effort_limit were rebalanced upward
         (3333->22000 N/m, 120->800 N, 3.0->20.0 N*m) to restore it - live-
         verified with the ACTUAL gripper payload attached (not just the
         bare bench, which understated the needed actuation budget by a
         real margin): a sustained 80deg step command settles at ~80-84deg,
         and the mission's own 0->80deg cosine sweep (5 cycles, under the
         45deg pitch) peaks consistently at 76-78deg. See
         continuum_arm_controller.py's ContinuumArmGains docstring for the
         matching closed-loop gain retune (curvature_scale/kp/ki) this
         actuation change also required. -->
    <plugin filename="RbsnArmController" name="rbsn_arm_controller::RbsnArmController">
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_1</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_2</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_3</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_4</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_5</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_6</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_7</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_8</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_9</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_10</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_11</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_12</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_13</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_14</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_15</joint_name>
      <pitch_radius>0.015</pitch_radius>
      <rest_length>0.4</rest_length>
      <tendon_stiffness>22000.0</tendon_stiffness>
      <max_tension>800.0</max_tension>
      <tendon_baseline>0.0</tendon_baseline>
      <k1>6.2</k1>
      <k2>0.0</k2>
      <c_theta>0.095</c_theta>
      <effort_limit>20.0</effort_limit>
      <tendon_topic>/continuum_arm_rbsn/tendon_cmd</tendon_topic>
      <command_filter_omega>2.92</command_filter_omega>
      <max_tendon_rate_m_s>0.06</max_tendon_rate_m_s>
    </plugin>

    <!-- Joint state feedback (actual, physics-integrated angles), same
         pattern rigid_arm_3link uses - lets the test script verify the arm
         actually bent the way the tendon command intended. -->
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-joint-state-publisher-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointStatePublisher">
      <topic>/continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_states</topic>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_1</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_2</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_3</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_4</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_5</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_6</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_7</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_8</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_9</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_10</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_11</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_12</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_13</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_14</joint_name>
      <joint_name>continuum_arm_rbsn/joint_15</joint_name>
    </plugin>

  </model>
</sdf>
